ROUTER VS SWITCH

+----------------------+------------------------------+------------------------------+
| FEATURE              | ROUTER                       | SWITCH                      |
+----------------------+------------------------------+------------------------------+
| 1. MAIN FUNCTION     | Connects different networks  | Connects devices within the  |
|                      | and forwards data between    | same local network (LAN).    |
|                      | them.                        |                              |
+----------------------+------------------------------+------------------------------+
| 2. ADDRESS USED      | Uses IP addresses to decide  | Uses MAC addresses to        |
|                      | where to send packets.       | forward data to the correct  |
|                      |                              | device.                      |
+----------------------+------------------------------+------------------------------+
| 3. NETWORK TRAFFIC   | Routes traffic between       | Forwards traffic between     |
|                      | different networks, such as  | devices on the same LAN,     |
|                      | a home LAN and the Internet. | usually to the required port.|
+----------------------+------------------------------+------------------------------+

KEY POINT:
Router = Uses IP addresses + Connects different networks
Switch = Uses MAC addresses + Connects devices in one LAN
